{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And on the day the Tabernacle was set up</b> — written seven times in the portion, corresponding to seven Tabernacles:" "<b>And at evening</b> — four times in the Masorah: here, and the others: \"And at evening you shall say, Who gives morning\"; \"burning offerings to YHWH… in the morning and at evening\"; and \"At evening I dug through the wall for myself\" in Ezekiel, who was prophesying about the exile. This is: \"At evening I dug through the wall for myself\" — when they went into exile, you will say: Who gives evening like that evening about which it says: \"burning offerings to YHWH in the morning and at evening\"; \"and as the appearance of fire until morning.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:42.671679182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}